<Project>
  <!-- The NuGet pin (owner-ruled 2026-10-05, landed in bump round 1): every tracked
       project restores from its committed packages.lock.json and ONLY from it.
       RestoreLockedMode turns a resolution that would differ from the lock — a
       moved reference, a new transitive version, a changed runtime id — into
       error NU1004 instead of a silent move, so a version changes only by a
       round's lockfile edit (docs/goal/architecture/release-integrity.md
       § Minimum release age for new dependency versions; dependency-bump-report.md
       § Who opens a round). Committed constants, never a per-machine knob.

       Conditioned on the lockfile being there, so a project with none (a scratch
       project a tool generates under this tree) is never forced into locked mode;
       a tracked project with none fails test_nuget_references_pinned.py instead.

       A round regenerates a lock deliberately, on a scratch copy: one restore with
       locked mode switched off and a forced re-evaluation, typed by hand — never
       committed to a recipe, script or workflow (the same test holds that). -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="Exists('$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)/packages.lock.json')">
    <RestorePackagesWithLockFile>true</RestorePackagesWithLockFile>
    <RestoreLockedMode>true</RestoreLockedMode>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
